  "header_text": "ABOUT OVERVIEW OF ECKERDVALUE OF LIBERAL ARTS ACADEMICS ACADEMICS OVERVIEWMAJORS & MINORSGLOBAL EDUCATION ADMISSION & AID ADMISSIONS OVERVIEWREQUEST MORE INFO ATHLETICS CAMPUS LIFE CAMPUS LIFE OVERVIEW GIVE & ENGAGE",
  "footer_text": "St. Petersburg, Florida 33711 +1 800.456.9009 +1 727.867.1166 Accessibility Directory Campus Map EASE Grant Performance Measures Jobs MyEckerd Portal Nondiscrimination Privacy Reporting Mechanisms © 2016-2026, Eckerd College, Inc. (non-profit). ECKERD COLLEGE® and Shell Design®.",
  "above_fold_text": "Find It Fast For the Public Newsroom About Overview of Eckerd Value of Liberal Arts Academics Academics Overview MAJORS & MINORS GLOBAL EDUCATION Admission & Aid Admissions Overview REQUEST MORE INFO Athletics Campus Life Campus Life Overview Give & Engage Peace Corps Prep Prepare yourself to make a real difference in the world This website uses cookies to provide a user better experience and for analytics. By clicking 'Accept' or continuing to use the site, you agree to our use of cookies as described in our privacy policy. Accept",
  "visible_text": "Skip to main content\nFind It Fast\nFor the Public\nNewsroom\nABOUT\nOVERVIEW OF ECKERDVALUE OF LIBERAL ARTS\nACADEMICS\nACADEMICS OVERVIEWMAJORS & MINORSGLOBAL EDUCATION\nADMISSION & AID\nADMISSIONS OVERVIEWREQUEST MORE INFO\nATHLETICS\nCAMPUS LIFE\nCAMPUS LIFE OVERVIEW\nGIVE & ENGAGE\nPEACE CORPS PREP\nPREPARE YOURSELF TO MAKE A REAL DIFFERENCE IN THE WORLD\nInterested in post-graduate experience or a career in international development? Attending Eckerd will make you more competitive.\n\nThe Eckerd Peace Corps Prep program combines targeted coursework with service-oriented field work and professional development training designed to make participants more competitive when applying for postgraduate Peace Corps volunteer positions, Fulbright U.S. Scholarships and other international development and intercultural fieldwork opportunities.\n\nEckerd College ranks No. 10 in the small college category among Peace Corps’ 2025 Top Volunteer-Producing Colleges and Universities list.\n\nFrom its inception in 1958, Eckerd College has emphasized global responsibility and citizenship as part of its liberal arts curriculum. As a result, more than 176 of our graduates have been inspired to serve in the Peace Corps or other international development organizations.\n\nWe attract students who are passionate about making a difference in the world. Peace Corps Prep provides a multifaceted pathway to focus idealism in practical ways and enhance personal, social, cultural and professional competence.\n\n176\n\nEckerd alumni have served or will soon serve in the Peace Corps since the organization’s inception in 1961\n\nPEACE CORPS VIDEOS\nFIND A RECRUITER\nVOLUNTEER OPENINGS\nHISTORY OF THE PEACE CORPS AT ECKERD\nService has always been a piece of the College mission.\n\nSince 1964, more than 175 Eckerd College graduates have served or will soon serve in the Peace Corps around the globe. Two members of the first graduating class left Florida to serve the Peace Corps in Costa Rica and Guatemala.\n\nStudent demand for opportunities to serve was so high the College began giving the Peace Corps Placement Test on campus in November of 1964. Recruiters commenced regular visits to Eckerd College during the Fall Semester in 1965.\n\nHow Peace Corps Prep works at Eckerd College\n\nAs part of their application to the Eckerd Peace Corps Prep program students will choose one of the following Peace Corps Work Sectors offered at Eckerd:\n\nAgriculture\nEducation\nEnvironment\nHealth\nYouth in Development\nCommunity Economic Development\n\nAccepted students will then work with the Eckerd Peace Corps Prep program advisors and their mentor to select approved courses, participate in service activities related to their sector, and document on- and off-campus leadership and professional development opportunities to complete the program.\n\nEckerd Peace Corps Prep students who complete all of the program requirements will receive a certificate of completion from Peace Corps after their graduation from Eckerd College and a notation on their Eckerd College transcript.\n\nApplying for Peace Corps Prep at Eckerd College\n\nOur Peace Corps Prep program is recommended for rising sophomores and juniors because of the strategic and program planning required; program application occurs annually in the spring semester.\n\nServing together\n\nRobert Little II ’11, a marine science and environmental studies graduate, and Stephanie Burkhardt ’11, a marine science graduate, are serving (as a couple) in Zambia, Africa, as Rural Aquaculture Promotion Volunteers and also working in other sectors through secondary projects and committees.\n\nPeace Corps questions?\n\nContact our program coordinator at epcprep@eckerd.edu.\n\nMORE ABOUT ECKERD PEACE CORPS PREP FOR CURRENT STUDENTS\n\nBanner photo: Timor-Leste, courtesy Peace Corps\n\nSt. Petersburg, Florida 33711\n+1 800.456.9009\n+1 727.867.1166\n\nAccessibility\nDirectory\nCampus Map\nEASE Grant Performance Measures\nJobs\nMyEckerd Portal\nNondiscrimination\nPrivacy\nReporting Mechanisms\n\n© 2016-2026, Eckerd College, Inc. (non-profit). ECKERD COLLEGE® and Shell Design®.\n\nThis website uses cookies to provide a user better experience and for analytics. By clicking 'Accept' or continuing to use the site, you agree to our use of cookies as described in our privacy policy.\n\nAccept",
